        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "How A Scan Runs"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "read summaries",
              "discard ranges",
              "scan survivors",
              "recheck tuples",
              "bitmap heap scan"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Lossy by design: never proves a row matches",
            "Only proves a block range might match",
            "So it is always a bitmap heap scan, never a plain index scan"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Only With Correlation"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "sql",
          "lines": [
            "SELECT attname, correlation FROM pg_stats",
            "WHERE tablename = 'events';",
            "-- want > 0.9 or < -0.9",
            "CREATE INDEX ON events USING brin (ts);"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Canonical fit: append-only time-series with a `created_at`",
            "Or a log table with a monotonically increasing id",
            "Anti-pattern: a `uuid` or hashed key, randomly distributed",
            "There every range matches, degenerating into a seq scan plus overhead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
